/* =========================================================================
   Bordeaux Dashboard — official appellation delimitations
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   PROVENANCE: VERIFIED, and openly licensed. These are the INAO’s own
   parcel delimitations for the Gironde, published on data.gouv.fr under
   the Licence Ouverte (Etalab), dissolved per appellation and simplified
   to the scale this map draws at.

   They replace the generalised outlines in geography.js, which covered
   whole communes: Margaux was drawn 3.2x its real extent, Pauillac 2.8x,
   and Moulis and Canon-Fronsac sat beside their true ground rather than
   on it. What is drawn now is the land actually entitled to the name —
   woods, villages and unsuitable soil excluded, which is why the shapes
   are ragged and come in several pieces.

   Blaye and Castillon are filed by INAO as denominations inside Côtes
   de Bordeaux rather than as appellations of their own, so they come
   from the denomination field; every region on the map is official.

   The official delimitation of record remains the plans deposited with
   the mairie or the INAO; this is a drawing of them, not a survey.

   ENCODING: "lat,lng" for the first point of a ring, then each later
   point as a delta in ten-thousandths of a degree. decodeRings() in
   app.js turns it back into [[lat,lng], ...].
   ========================================================================= */

